IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eca-nouns`
IMPORT `eca-schedules`
IMPORT `eca-part1-preliminary`
IMPORT `eca-part3-jurisdiction`

-- Tests of Part 3, Divisions 1 and 2 (ss 9, 11 to 17).  Every expected value was decided from the text before the run and is written beside its assertion.
-- Amounts, limits, fees and periods are arbitrary test values: the Act fixes none of them.

-- fixtures: matters
`first sch item 17` MEANS `A matter in the First Schedule` `Salary in lieu of notice of termination`
`first sch item 16` MEANS `A matter in the First Schedule` `Salary`
`second sch item 13` MEANS `A matter in the Second Schedule` `Item 13: employee's payment where the employer ends the contract of service without notice (EA 1968 s 11(1))`
`second sch item 14` MEANS `A matter in the Second Schedule` `Item 14: employer's payment where the employee ends the contract of service without notice (EA 1968 s 11(1))`
`second sch item 15` MEANS `A matter in the Second Schedule` `Item 15: employee's payment where the employer breaks the contract of service (EA 1968 s 16)`
`second sch item 16` MEANS `A matter in the Second Schedule` `Item 16: employer's payment where the employee breaks the contract of service (EA 1968 s 16)`
`second sch item 17` MEANS `A matter in the Second Schedule` `Item 17: employee's payment of salary (EA 1968 s 21, 22 or 23)`
`third sch item 1` MEANS `A matter in the Third Schedule` `Item 1: dismissal without just cause or excuse, where the employee may claim under EA 1968 s 14(2)`

§ `Tests -- ss 9 and 11`

#ASSERT `s 9(6) the individual may sit as a tribunal magistrate in relation to the case` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(6) the individual may sit as a tribunal magistrate in relation to the case` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- a case the individual did not hear
#ASSERT `s 9(6) the individual may sit as a tribunal magistrate in relation to the case` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING  -- never appointed or designated
#ASSERT `s 11(3) the registrar for the tribunals may exercise the jurisdiction and powers of a tribunal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11(3) the registrar for the tribunals may exercise the jurisdiction and powers of a tribunal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(4) the officer may exercise and perform the powers and duties of the registrar for the tribunals` `A deputy registrar` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11(4) the officer may exercise and perform the powers and duties of the registrar for the tribunals` `An assistant registrar` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11(4) the officer may exercise and perform the powers and duties of the registrar for the tribunals` `The registrar` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11(4) the officer may exercise and perform the powers and duties of the registrar for the tribunals` `Another officer` EQUALS NOTHING

