#ASSERT `s 12(2)(a) the claim is made by an employee in a prescribed class against the employer` `A person entitled under a written law to receive the amount claimed in place of the employee` `The employer of the employee` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12(2)(a) the claim is made by an employee in a prescribed class against the employer` `The employee` `The employer of the employee` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- not a prescribed class
#ASSERT `s 12(2)(a) the claim is made by an employee in a prescribed class against the employer` `The employee` `The employer of the employee` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING  -- the classes are outside the sources
#ASSERT `s 12(2)(a) the claim is made by an employee in a prescribed class against the employer` `The employee` `A person liable under section 65 of the Employment Act 1968 for the employee's salary` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- not against the employer
#ASSERT `s 12(2)(a) the claim is made by an employee in a prescribed class against the employer` `The employer` `An employee of the employer` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

